@startuml
skinparam monochrome true

title Force Event Register for Error Interrupt Status (Offset 052h)

note as N1
**Register Bit Layout (D15-D00)**
|= D15-D12 |= D11-D10 |= D09 |= D08 |= D07 |= D06 |= D05 |= D04 |= D03 |= D02 |= D01 |= D00 |
| Force Event for Vendor Specific Error Status | Rsvd | Force Event for ADMA Error | Force Event for Auto CMD Error | Force Event for Current limit Error | Force Event for Data End Bit Error | Force Event for Data CRC Error | Force Event for Data Timeout Error | Force Event for Command Index Error | Force Event for Command End Bit Error | Force Event for Command CRC Error | Force Event for Command Timeout Error |
end note

|= Location |= Attrib |= Register Field Explanation |
| 15-12 | WO | **Force Event for Vendor Specific Error Status**\nAdditional status bits can be defined in this register by the vendor.\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 11-10 | Rsvd | **Reserved** |
| 09 | WO | **Force Event for ADMA Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 08 | WO | **Force Event for Auto CMD Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 07 | WO | **Force Event for Current Limit Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 06 | WO | **Force Event for Data End Bit Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 05 | WO | **Force Event for Data CRC Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 04 | WO | **Force Event for Data Timeout Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 03 | WO | **Force Event for Command Index Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 02 | WO | **Force Event for Command End Bit Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 01 | WO | **Force Event for Command CRC Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |
| 00 | WO | **Force Event for Command Timeout Error**\n1 = Interrupt is generated\n0 = No Interrupt |

note as N2
**Register Behavior:**
- This is not a physically implemented register
- Writing to this address is reflected in Error Interrupt Status Register
- Writing 1: Sets corresponding bit in Error Interrupt Status Register
- Writing 0: No effect
- Both Error Interrupt Status Enable and Error Interrupt Signal Enable must be set to generate interrupt
end note

@enduml